WEBVTT

00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,210
Are you familiar with Dr. Thomas Sigfried?

00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:12,650
Yes.

00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,730
What are your thoughts on him say that no tumor considered

00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:22,810
five if you're in ketosis, no glucose, and glutamine?

00:00:22,810 --> 00:00:25,570
Well, the only thing I don't like about his book he wrote

00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:28,970
was at the metabolic, something of cancer

00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:30,610
or something like that.

00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:32,170
He doesn't practice.

00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,930
He's just a researcher.

00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:37,770
So he doesn't actually seek cancer patients.

00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:42,890
It is book he only had an example of one cancer patient

00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,530
who had smoldering multiple myeloma.

00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:51,330
It's not a good example as having one decay study

00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:53,370
to work through with your book.

00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:57,730
And I am totally in agreement that many times,

00:00:57,730 --> 00:01:01,890
especially if you have HIF1G defects,

00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:05,570
and you're going to be way more prone for your cancer

00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:09,250
to be feeding on the end stage of glycolysis,

00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:13,010
just feeding off of lactic acid, because you don't convert

00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:16,650
lactic acid into acetyl coenzyme, very quickly,

00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:20,130
that going on a more ketogenic diet can be helpful.

00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:22,730
So if nobody's read his book except the person

00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:26,010
who asked the question, he thinks every cancer patient

00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:28,570
should call it a ketogenic diet.

00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:32,890
And to me, whenever anybody says a comment like that,

00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:35,570
it's an instant red flag, because every human being

00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:37,530
is different, every cancer is different.

00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:39,330
I don't care if you and your twin brother

00:01:39,330 --> 00:01:41,570
have colon cancer, it can be completely different

00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:43,130
in your two bodies.

00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:47,810
So it's just not, when you make blanket statements like that,

00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:53,770
to me, it shows a little bit of ignorance in real life practice.

00:01:53,770 --> 00:01:58,210
So I guess that's all I'd say about that.

00:01:58,210 --> 00:01:59,410
I just disagree with that.

00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:01,490
I think everybody is different.

00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:06,250
Some people's bodies, their cancer speed

00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:08,410
totally different than other people.

00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:10,610
So I just don't necessarily agree with it.

00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:12,610
I was too told through your genetic testing

00:02:12,610 --> 00:02:14,290
that a keto diet would be good for me.

00:02:14,290 --> 00:02:17,170
OK, so who's asking this question?

00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:20,170
I don't remember your genetics.

00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:23,970
You may have a lot of HIF1 gene defects.

00:02:23,970 --> 00:02:27,450
So going on a ketogenic diet is something you could do.

00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:30,130
And you don't have to go full ketogenic

00:02:30,130 --> 00:02:31,370
and get into ketosis.

00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:35,730
You could just do a modified ketogenic diet.

00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:39,570
That's where intermittent fasting can

00:02:39,570 --> 00:02:41,850
be super beneficial for people.

00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:44,050
So I probably recommended intermittent fasting

00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:45,250
for you as well.

